==English==

===Etymology===
Named for its founder, [[w:Sir George Downing, 1st Baronet|Sir George Downing]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-Downing Street.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[Downing]] [[street|Street]]}}

# A [[street]] leading off [[Whitehall]] in [[Westminster]], [[London]] containing the [[residence]]s of the [[Prime Minister]] and the [[Chancellor of the Exchequer]]
# {{lb|en|metonymic|by extension}} The [[British]] [[government]].
# {{lb|en|loosely}} Either [[10 Downing Street]] or [[11 Downing Street]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2024 January 10|author=Christian Wolmar|title=A time for change? ... just as it was back in issue 262|journal=RAIL|issue=1000|page=60|text=For all his faults and grandstanding, however, Prescott genuinely cared - and his ambitious plans for tram schemes and railway extensions were stymied by lack of support from '''Downing Street'''.}}

